<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The Group recorded bad debt expenses of RMB <ix:nonFraction contextRef="c17" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:FinancingReceivableAllowanceForCreditLossesRecovery" scale="0" unitRef="cny" id="ixv-12822">211,962</ix:nonFraction>
and <span style="-sec-ix-hidden: hidden-fact-111">nil</span> for the the six months ended June 30, 2024 and 2025, respectively. For the six months ended June 30, 2024 and 2025, the Group
had written off <span style="-sec-ix-hidden: hidden-fact-112">nil</span> and RMB <ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="jyd:FinancingReceivableAllowanceForCreditLossesWriteOff" scale="0" unitRef="cny" id="ixv-12823">5,378</ix:nonFraction> (US$<ix:nonFraction contextRef="c0" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="jyd:FinancingReceivableAllowanceForCreditLossesWriteOff" scale="0" unitRef="usd" id="ixv-12824">751</ix:nonFraction>) in bad debt, respectively.</p></ix:continuation><div>

