</div><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c0" continuedAt="_ShortTermDebtTextBlock-c0_cont_1" escape="true" name="us-gaap:ShortTermDebtTextBlock" id="ixv-6697"><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><b>8. SHORT-TERM BORROWINGS</b></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&#160;</p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">Short-term borrowings represent amounts due to
various banks normally maturing within <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c0" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="jyd:ShorttermBorrowingsMaturitiePeriod" id="ixv-12908">one year</ix:nonNumeric>. The principal of the borrowings is due at maturity. Accrued interest is due either monthly
or quarterly. The bank borrowings are for working capital and capital expenditure purposes. <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="c0" continuedAt="_ScheduleOfShortTermDebtTextBlock-c0_cont_1" escape="true" name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfShortTermDebtTextBlock" id="ixv-12909">The balance of short-term borrowings consists
of the following:</ix:nonNumeric></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&#160;</p>

<ix:continuation continuedAt="_ScheduleOfShortTermDebtTextBlock-c0_cont_2" id="_ScheduleOfShortTermDebtTextBlock-c0_cont_1"><table cellpadding="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; border-spacing: 0px;">
